<h2 id="faq-heading">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="usa-accordion usa-accordion--bordered usa-accordion--multiselectable" data-allow-multiple="">
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-1">What is a wire mesh belt conveyor?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-1" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>A wire mesh belt conveyor uses an open-weave metal belt that allows airflow, drainage, and heat transfer through the conveying surface. Essential for ovens, freezers, washdown systems, and drying tunnels. Belt materials range from carbon steel to high-nickel alloys such as Inconel 601, which The Furnace Belt Company rates to 2,100°F.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-2">What temperature can a wire mesh belt handle?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-2" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>The Furnace Belt Company lists these maximum operating temperatures: plain carbon steel 600°F, high-carbon steel 1,050°F, 304 and 316 stainless 1,500°F, 314 stainless 2,050°F, and Inconel 601 and 80/20 nickel-chrome 2,100°F. Allowable belt tension drops sharply as temperature rises, so size the belt for the operating temperature. Stainless mesh is also used in spiral freezers.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-3">What are the main wire mesh belt weave types?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-3" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Balanced weave (spiral + cross rod, general purpose), compound balanced (closely nested spirals for small products), and chain-driven mesh (roller chains on edges for heavy loads and high temps). Flat wire and woven wire cloth serve specialty coating and fine-particle applications.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-4">How do you clean a wire mesh conveyor belt?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-4" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>CIP spray bars clean both belt surfaces during operation. Weekly deep cleaning includes releasing tension, alkaline soaking, and brushing cross rod junctions. Automated belt washers with rotating brushes handle daily sanitation in food plants. Bottom sprays are critical for removing debris from the return side.</p>

</div>
</div>
